  "dom_id": "step-q72479",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- ${P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},\u2026,{x}_{m}}$ is a partition of the interval $[2,4]$\n\n- ${P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},\u2026,{y}_{n}}$ is a partition of the interval $[3,7]$\n\nCalculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}5\u0394{x}_{i}\u0394{y}_{j},$ where $\u0394{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $\u0394{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1}.$",
  "worked_solution": "Using the constant multiple and product rules, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}5\u0394{x}_{i}\u0394{y}_{j} & =5{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\u0394{x}_{i}\u0394{y}_{j} \\\\  & =5{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}\u0394{x}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\u0394{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}\u0394{x}_{i}$ and ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\u0394{y}_{j}$ are just the lengths of the intervals $[2,4]$ and $[3,7]$ respectively. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}\u0394{x}_{i} & =4-2=2, \\\\ {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\u0394{y}_{j} & =7-3=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we have\n\n$$\n5{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}\u0394{x}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\u0394{y}_{j}=5\\cdot 2\\cdot 4=40.\n$$",
